--TEST--
`break` leaves a loop, so it is offered where a loop is around the cursor with no function body in between, and the same method's body outside the loop is not offered it — `rule:ide/keywords-are-offered-where-the-compiler-accepts-them`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Cart {
    public function total(): int {
        while (true) {
            b<|>r;
        }
        return 1;
    }
}
--REQUEST--
completion prefix=b
--EXPECT--
break   keyword
